From 92c22271e8145ace4232f95cfd39696399e3df08 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cam <cmayberry35@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 00:00:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Tighter towers, Voidmaw at the top of the map, and a
 predicted local champion

Map: Voidmaw now broods in a web at the very top centre, reached by two ramps
from the left and right of the lane below it. The top lane sags deeper under
the web and the northern jungle moved down to make room, taking the wraith and
wolf camps with it. The old hollow is now an ordinary jungle pocket.

Towers: range 620 -> 520 (Ancient 640 -> 560) for a threat circle closer to
League's, with champion attack ranges scaled to match so towers still outrange
everyone: Sylvane 550 -> 460, Tinka 540 -> 470, Vesper 520 -> 450, Marrowin and
Oryn 500 -> 440, Galewind Cannon +50 -> +40, Tinka's turret 470 -> 420. Minion
casters and siege minions also shoot from closer so lanes sit inside tower
cover. 120 simulated matches put every champion between 38% and 59%.

Online feel: your own champion is now simulated locally and reconciled against
the server each snapshot, so it answers the mouse in ~50ms instead of waiting a
round trip (measured drift from the server: 4px median, 16px worst). Ability
icons start their cooldown on the keypress. Snapshots only carry units whose
state actually changed, which cut traffic from 19 KB/s to 11 KB/s per player.

Also restores offline/shardfall.html, the single-file single-player build.

